  "summary": [
    "Batch A, family A1 (`induced_free`). Ten conjecture-local helpers, all `forall S : {set G}, ~ inhabited (induced S ≃ H)` (X41 as `x41_induced_H_free H G`), now unfold to `GTBase.common.induced_free G H`; the X41 alias keeps its `(H G)` argument order. Every frozen body below is checked against the source text at its commit, and every certificate theorem is kernel-checked by `meta/check_library_migration.py` (Print Assumptions clean).",
    "",
    "Ten statements are affected (X41, X42, X43, X56, X57, X58, X61, X102, X118, X120), three of them through an intermediate helper (`x57_sparse_strong_eh_property`, `x61_induced_saturated`, `x102_free_class_tree_alpha_bounded`). Each frozen statement resolves through frozen copies along the whole affected chain. Declarations outside the chain resolve through their live definitions, which this migration does not change. Three of those were redirected earlier by M1: `x43_edge_set`, `x60_edge_set` and `x102_edge_set`. For X61 and X102 an end-to-end certificate also freezes M1's edge-set presentation, so it relates the pre-M1, pre-A1 statement body to the live one. For X43, M1 left only the alias-level certificate `Chromatic.migration.simple_edges.x43_edge_set_compat`: the dependent transport through `x43_line_graph` is not certified at statement level, by M1 or here.",
    "",
    "No statement text, doc block, manifest row or leg state changes (checked below). The documented discrepancies and restrictions of the affected rows therefore stay verbatim: X41 and X58 bound the A side only near-linearly, weaker than the source; X42 encodes only the treewidth half (row partial); X43 omits the T(G) phrasing; X56 allows only reciprocal-integer exponents; X61 reads an infinite family as members of unbounded size; X102 approximates subdivided multiclaws.",
    "",
    "The two discovery-only name matches stay distinct and untouched. `x207_H_free` is minor exclusion and is documented in X207.v as the WRONG OBJECT for that source (the row is BLOCKED). Repairing it is a separate re-audit, not part of this migration."
  ],
